<title>SINGAPORE: Goldtron 1996 net profit falls 2.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Goldtron 1996 net profit falls 2.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   22.69   vs	23.27</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)		     11.00   vs	 4.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   6.00   vs	 6.90</p>
<p>    Turnover			    574.51   vs     553.38</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest     1.17   vs	 1.13</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		 10.09   vs	 7.84</p>
<p>    Depreciation			 23.44   vs	14.60</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	  12.56   vs	 9.83</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     20.26   vs	19.28</p>
<p>    Tax				     7.84   vs	 5.08</p>
<p>    Minorities			   (2.28)  vs	 0.76</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		     4.79   vs     (19.33)</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: July 23, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: July 9, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Goldtron Ltd is an electronics manufacturer.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
